                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Highly Recommend : 8/10 (Interesting Story, Detail and Huge Game World \n\nI love RPG Maker Games, but lately most of the RPG Maker games that I have played are just slightly above mediocre. However, I would highly recommend this game and even though it is a bit pricey. I paid full price of $8, but it is definitely worth it.\n\nThis game have nice graphics, and a very interesting story line. It almost feel like a huge open world game, with a lot of detective-style puzzle solving. The hero also engaged in livefly banter. Despite being quite egoistical, the heroes and his group are quite endearing. \n\nA good game is nothing without great game mechanics and lots of grindings. This game have both. I also like the way money are tightly control, so that you will not have enough money to always buy the things you want. Non human monsters do not drop gold/money, which make it all the more compelling to do all the little secondary quests. The quests are all well thought out and require quite a bit of problem solving too. \n\nThere are also various hidden variables like Karma, Friendship, etc that are not visible to you, but will indirectly affect you in this game. This helps to keep me on my toes, and read each conversation carefully and pick the best decision. However, since you may not see the consequences of your decision immediately, and  you cannot inspect the hidden variables, this add tension and suspence to the game. I love it, and actually keep multiple save games.\n\nAnyway, I am going back to my game. Check out this game if you are an old school RPG gamer like me.\n\n",
